:: Millers Babysitting Backyard Ask to Play 2 [nobr]

/* Intro */
You find <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> sitting on one of the lounge chairs near the pool, the boy’s small body dwarfed by the adult-sized chair. He is quietly singing to himself while fiddling with the material of the chair. <span style="Color: LightGreen">You ask him if he wants to play a game and he quickly perks up,</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oh yeah! Let’s play hide-and-seek! You stay here and count to 20 and I’ll hide and you have to find me. Oh, but only back here. No going inside, to make it easier for you.”</span> He smirks as you agree and sit down on the patio to begin counting. You hear the sound of him rushing off as you count loudly, though try to listen to hear where he may be heading. 

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Smirk",
                Eyes: "Tired",
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

About 20 seconds later, you call out that, ready or not, you are coming! You open your eyes to find the backyard empty, from what you can see from a glance anyway. Not bad, the kid at least found a place out of sight to hide. Now, considering the size of this yard, it may be hard to find him. But the yard is also pretty open without a lot of places even someone of his small stature could conceal himself. <span style="Color: Yellow">That leaves you with two obvious options. Behind the shed and under the deck.</span> <br>
<br>

<<set _kaydenLocation to random(1, 2)>>
